{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:adapted-frame-smooth","title":"lem:adapted-frame-smooth","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":1726,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#lem:adapted-frame-smooth","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-normal-at]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:pushforward-smooth]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:unit-normal]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"lem:adapted-frame-smooth","line":2861,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[The Adapted Frame Varies Smoothly]\n\\label{lem:adapted-frame-smooth}\n\n\\uses{def:smooth-normal-at, lem:pushforward-smooth, def:unit-normal, lem:ambient-tangent-bundle-riemannian}\n\n\n\n\nIf $N$ varies smoothly along an immersion $F:M\\to\\widetilde M$ and $(E_i)$ is a smooth local frame of $TM$, every member of $(N,dFE_1,\\ldots,dFE_n)$ is a smooth section of $F^*T\\widetilde M$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{def:smooth-normal-at,lem:pushforward-smooth}\n\\sketch $N$ is smooth by hypothesis and each $dF(E_i)$ is smooth by the pushforward-smoothness lemma.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[The Adapted Frame Varies Smoothly] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a616461707465642d6672616d652d736d6f6f7468\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Asmooth-normal-at\">↗ def:smooth-normal-at</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannia